        form: '<table><tr><th>Pattern</th><th>Verbs</th><th>Example</th></tr><tr><td>verb + to + infinitive</td><td>agree, refuse, offer, promise, threaten</td><td>Carl offered to deliver twice a month. They refused to lower the price.</td></tr><tr><td>verb + object + to + infinitive</td><td>ask, advise, warn, remind, encourage, persuade</td><td>She asked him to send the contract. He warned us not to sign yet.</td></tr><tr><td>verb + -ing</td><td>suggest, recommend, admit, deny</td><td>Ana suggested meeting halfway. He denied making a mistake.</td></tr><tr><td>verb + that + clause</td><td>suggest, recommend, insist, admit, explain, agree</td><td>She suggested that we (should) meet halfway. He insisted that the price was fair.</td></tr><tr><td>verb + preposition + -ing</td><td>insist on, apologize for, blame … for, accuse … of</td><td>He insisted on getting the contract by Friday.</td></tr></table><p class="small"><b>suggest</b> never takes object + to: not “suggested me to…”.</p>',
